"`cost_sensitivity_v_FA/FB/RB/RA.py`, all `--executables-dir Executables`"
msgstr ""
"`cost_sensitivity_v_SR_WF.py`, luego `nli_sr_recompute.py`, luego "
"`cost_sensitivity_v_FA/FB/RB/RA.py`, todos con `--executables-dir "
"Executables`"

#: ../../pipeline.md:381
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`scripts/tx_chain/cost_sensitivity_v_SR_WF.py`, `nli_sr_recompute.py`, "
"`cost_sensitivity_v_{FA,FB,RB,RA}.py`"
msgstr ""
"`scripts/tx_chain/cost_sensitivity_v_SR_WF.py`, `nli_sr_recompute.py`, "
"`cost_sensitivity_v_{FA,FB,RB,RA}.py`"

#: ../../pipeline.md:381
msgid ""
"BSR, ISR, VSR, ISRWF, VSRWF (new scenarios); ISR/VSR/ISRWF/VSRWF edited "
"in place; BFA/IFA, BFB/IFB, BRB/IRB, BRA/IRA (cost sensitivities from "
"BAC/INV)"
msgstr ""
"BSR, ISR, VSR, ISRWF, VSRWF (escenarios nuevos); ISR/VSR/ISRWF/VSRWF "
"editados en el lugar; BFA/IFA, BFB/IFB, BRB/IRB, BRA/IRA (sensibilidades "
"de costo a partir de BAC/INV)"

#: ../../pipeline.md:395
msgid ""
"Extensibility: a new constraint script or derived scenario is added "
"entirely in `Config_MOMF_T1_AB.yaml` -- a `scenario_transforms` entry "
"(script + `produces`/`in_place`) plus a `derived_scenarios` mapping and, "
"if it should be solved, an entry in `solve_scenarios`. No B2 code change "
"is needed."
msgstr ""
"Extensibilidad: un nuevo script de restricciones o escenario derivado se "
"agrega completamente en `Config_MOMF_T1_AB.yaml` -- una entrada de "
"`scenario_transforms` (script + `produces`/`in_place`) más un mapeo en "
"`derived_scenarios` y, si debe resolverse, una entrada en "
"`solve_scenarios`. No se necesita ningún cambio de código en B2."

#: ../../pipeline.md:397
msgid ""
"Solve universe: `solve_universe()` resolves `solve_scenarios` from the "
"YAML (defaulting to the base scenarios) and validates each has its final "
"datafile before the solver stage runs; `scenario_base()` maps a derived "
"scenario back to the base whose A2/sets it reuses for otoole results."
msgstr ""
"Universo de resolución: `solve_universe()` resuelve `solve_scenarios` "
"desde el YAML (por defecto los escenarios base) y valida que cada uno "
"tenga su archivo de datos final antes de que se ejecute la etapa del "
"solver; `scenario_base()` mapea un escenario derivado de vuelta a la base"
" cuyo A2/conjuntos reutiliza para los resultados de otoole."

#: ../../pipeline.md:399
msgid "Scenario codes (shipped `Config_MOMF_T1_AB.yaml`, 2026-09-17)"
msgstr "Códigos de escenario (`Config_MOMF_T1_AB.yaml` de fábrica, 2026-09-17)"

#: ../../pipeline.md:401
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Base scenarios are the four `A1_Outputs_<S>/` folders: **BAU, INV, OPT, "
"VGB**. Every other code is derived by the Tx chain. Reading a code: first"
" letter `B` = optimal family (built on BAU/BAC), `I` = trend family "
"(built on INV/ISR); suffixes `SR` = no repowering, `FA`/`FB` = fossil "
"fuel cost high/low, `RA`/`RB` = renewables cost high/low, `WF` = water-"
"fill NLI weights. Report names (see {doc}`study/scenarios`): OPT = BAC, "
"ETT = ISR, PLAN = OPC, ETT-GP = VSR."
msgstr ""
"Los escenarios base son las cuatro carpetas `A1_Outputs_<S>/`: **BAU, "
"INV, OPT, VGB**. Cualquier otro código es derivado por la cadena Tx. Cómo"
" leer un código: la primera letra `B` = familia óptima (construida sobre "
"BAU/BAC), `I` = familia de tendencia (construida sobre INV/ISR); sufijos "
"`SR` = sin repotenciación, `FA`/`FB` = costo de combustible fósil "
"alto/bajo, `RA`/`RB` = costo de renovables alto/bajo, `WF` = pesos NLI de"
" water-fill. Nombres de reporte (ver {doc}`study/scenarios`): OPT = BAC, "
"ETT = ISR, PLAN = OPC, ETT-GP = VSR."

